WEBVTT

00:01:57.923 --> 00:02:02.133
It's the same problem with giving animals
small and regular doses of antibiotics:

00:02:02.157 --> 00:02:04.839
some bad bugs die but not all of them.

00:02:04.863 --> 00:02:07.276
Spread that across an entire industry,

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.768
and you can understand
that we accidentally build up

00:02:09.792 --> 00:02:13.339
a large reservoir
of antibiotic-resistant bacteria.

00:02:15.006 --> 00:02:16.560
But I hate to break it to you --

00:02:16.584 --> 00:02:18.651
the problem doesn't stop there.

00:02:18.998 --> 00:02:21.656
You know who else takes antibiotics?

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.921
Fluffy, your cat, and Rover, your dog.

00:02:23.945 --> 00:02:25.064
(Laughter)

00:02:25.088 --> 00:02:28.415
Pets rank even amongst
the heaviest users of all,

00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:29.832
and they use antibiotics

00:02:29.856 --> 00:02:32.148
that are much more critical
for human health.